used on trevor  milton nicolas frontman  and just a week later the founder and  executive chairman  resigned from the company's board  following the news shares of the eevee  startup  plunged even further just days later  reports surfaced that nicholas talks  with partners to build hydrogen stations  had stalled  in the few weeks after the report came  out on september 10th nicola  lost about 45 percent of its market cap  uh the partnership that it had announced  on september  8th with general motors uh was supposed  to close at the end of september and has  not yet closed it's started to affect  nikola's ability to  attract and retain partners but at this  key moment nikola doubled down  the company reiterated its business plan  and some milestones that it expects to  hit  over the next few years um and really  kind of  reasserted uh that that it's focused  right now on  execution of its business plan in a  post-trevor milton era  following this news the truck maker's  stock price began to slightly recover  and its new leadership seemed confident  the company's been public for what four  months  um so you know we're comfortable with  the diligence we did  a lot of analysts have actually  reiterated that they do believe in  nicola  um and that they ultimately see that the  the moving on from trevor milton as a  good thing  for the company in the long run um but a  lot of those analysts too have written  about you know nicolas kind of need to  reestablish credibility  even though customers have yet to flock  to electric vehicles  big auto companies and investors are  betting they will soon  fueling an interest in showy startups  like nikola the fact that the markets  can both be  so quickly taken with a company like  nikola and then  quickly kind of disenchanted with that  company  in a matter of months is kind of a  cautionary tale of some of the  enthusiasm around  electric vehicle startups and and kind  of  betting betting it all in the future  with new leadership